(5258376, 763803, 52549, '<td valign="top">This is stunning! Love the blues, the crispness, the dreaminess.... well, everything. Big congrats on your blue, Hugo.</td>', 'This is stunning! Love the blues, the crispness, the dreaminess.... well, everything. Big congrats on your blue, Hugo.', '2009-02-16 00:53:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258379, 763640, 52549, '<td valign="top">One of the really brilliant takes on the original. GREAT shot, Andreas and MOST deserving of a ribbon. Congrats.</td>', 'One of the really brilliant takes on the original. GREAT shot, Andreas and MOST deserving of a ribbon. Congrats.', '2009-02-16 00:54:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258383, 763644, 52549, '<td valign="top">Great blues, wonderful shot. Congrats on 4th.</td>', 'Great blues, wonderful shot. Congrats on 4th.', '2009-02-16 00:57:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258389, 763923, 63633, '<td valign="top">This is really beautiful Judi</td>', 'This is really beautiful Judi', '2009-02-16 01:02:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258403, 763846, 63633, '<td valign="top">Enzo you know I love your food photos - I gave this a 7. I do agree with the voters though in that this one doesn''t have as much impact as your usual stuff. <br/> <br/>I love the composition and the complimentary elements (wine, cutlery etc), but I think the exposure of the meat is a bit off, and so gives the impression that the pork is undercooked. I think some ingredients do high-key well, but meat doesn''t. <br/> <br/>When I do meat photography I tend use a browning agent to make the meat look more cooked (but don''t actually cook it longer, as it makes it look dried out).  browning essence mixed with a bit of olive oil gives a good colour and glisten, but still leaves it edible (Angostura bitters mixed with dishwashing detergent looks better, but some people actually like to eat their food when they are finished shooting it!) I think with pork you would need to go lightly with the colour, but it still needs something.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Enzo you know I love your food photos - I gave this a 7. I do agree with the voters though in that this one doesn''t have as much impact as your usual stuff.  I love the composition and the complimentary elements (wine, cutlery etc), but I think the exposure of the meat is a bit off, and so gives the impression that the pork is undercooked. I think some ingredients do high-key well, but meat doesn''t.  When I do meat photography I tend use a browning agent to make the meat look more cooked (but don''t actually cook it longer, as it makes it look dried out).  browning essence mixed with a bit of olive oil gives a good colour and glisten, but still leaves it edible (Angostura bitters mixed with dishwashing detergent looks better, but some people actually like to eat their food when they are finished shooting it!) I think with pork you would need to go lightly with the colour, but it still needs something. ', '2009-02-16 01:12:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258413, 763072, 53964, '<td valign="top">I was going to say that you are the master but I see that posthumous has already elevated you to the rank of god, so I''ll have to go with that instead :)</td>', 'I was going to say that you are the master but I see that posthumous has already elevated you to the rank of god, so I''ll have to go with that instead :)', '2009-02-16 01:26:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258415, 763397, 68504, '<td valign="top">Yikes!  Brilliant. Too too bad about the dq.</td>', 'Yikes!  Brilliant. Too too bad about the dq.', '2009-02-16 01:27:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258425, 763803, 78196, '<td valign="top">Hahaha, I always wanted to appear on the front page. Really good work - glad my intentionally awful entry was an ''inspiration''. :)</td>', 'Hahaha, I always wanted to appear on the front page. Really good work - glad my intentionally awful entry was an ''inspiration''. :)', '2009-02-16 01:38:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258427, 763809, 68504, '<td valign="top">Okay, that''s good for all that he isn''t stuffed, and my, he does seem glad to see you!</td>', 'Okay, that''s good for all that he isn''t stuffed, and my, he does seem glad to see you!', '2009-02-16 01:40:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258431, 763793, 96751, '<td valign="top">LOL!  Never thought of taking the shot first then trying to find a brownie "match"!!!  I really like the colors in your shot and the silhouettes.  I''ve stopped trying to figure out the whys and wherefores of voting; just do the best I can, and learning a lot from the comments and the work of really great photogs on this site.  See ya next round!</td>', 'LOL!  Never thought of taking the shot first then trying to find a brownie "match"!!!  I really like the colors in your shot and the silhouettes.  I''ve stopped trying to figure out the whys and wherefores of voting; just do the best I can, and learning a lot from the comments and the work of really great photogs on this site.  See ya next round!', '2009-02-16 01:55:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5258460, 763640, 31889, '<td valign="top">Well done and gratz on another ribbon. <br/> <br/>Interesting that you credited JoeyL when he himself borrowed the idea from Dave Hill.  Maybe Dave should get some credit too. :)</td>', 'Well done and gratz on another ribbon.  Interesting that you credited JoeyL when he himself borrowed the idea from Dave Hill.  Maybe Dave should get some credit too. :)', '2009-02-16 02:59:32.000000', NULL, 0),
