(5262141, 762566, 4226, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Looking at the original image, this has a big improvement. the lighting is much softer and overall has a soothing feel to it. <br/> <br/>My eyes keep searching for more in this image, I would have loved to see some more and not cropped so abruptly at the top. Also I don''t see a reason to use a shallower depth of field here. the blur on the foreground subjects is distracting IMO. <br/> <br/>For the same image, I would think a deeper depth of field will help. Also sharpening after resizing would make things better here. <br/> <br/>Please feel free to contact for any questions you have.<br/> <br/>-Gaurawa</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Looking at the original image, this has a big improvement. the lighting is much softer and overall has a soothing feel to it.  My eyes keep searching for more in this image, I would have loved to see some more and not cropped so abruptly at the top. Also I don''t see a reason to use a shallower depth of field here. the blur on the foreground subjects is distracting IMO.  For the same image, I would think a deeper depth of field will help. Also sharpening after resizing would make things better here.  Please feel free to contact for any questions you have. -Gaurawa', '2009-02-18 02:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
