(5266551, 763640, 104066, '<td valign="top">Great picture! More flying liquids would look amazing, but Jorge probably wasn''t up for it!</td>', 'Great picture! More flying liquids would look amazing, but Jorge probably wasn''t up for it!', '2009-02-20 16:54:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5267561, 763702, 47852, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/><u>First Impression</u>: A nice macro with good focus on the eyes.  I like that you can still see a bit of detail on the legs.  Nice lines with the branch and legs to fill out the photo, but I feel like the wings should be spread out on either side of the head... guess it was just the angle you took this at.<br/> <br/><u>Looking Closer</u>:  The contrast is good here, and you definitely have a full range of black to white in the head, but the rest of the photo seems to lack... something as far as the tones.  Looking at the photo you were copying, I can vaguely see the connection but it also seems a bit of a stretch.  I don''t know if adding the ID number of the copied photo in your title would have helped, or hurt.  It certainly took a creative eye to find something within that photo to replicate!<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful!  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions or comments.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  First Impression: A nice macro with good focus on the eyes.  I like that you can still see a bit of detail on the legs.  Nice lines with the branch and legs to fill out the photo, but I feel like the wings should be spread out on either side of the head... guess it was just the angle you took this at. Looking Closer:  The contrast is good here, and you definitely have a full range of black to white in the head, but the rest of the photo seems to lack... something as far as the tones.  Looking at the photo you were copying, I can vaguely see the connection but it also seems a bit of a stretch.  I don''t know if adding the ID number of the copied photo in your title would have helped, or hurt.  It certainly took a creative eye to find something within that photo to replicate! Hope this has been helpful!  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions or comments.', '2009-02-21 11:50:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(5268199, 763890, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I like that this is not centered, and that you have not "cut off" any of the drain (though that can work sometimes).  However, it seems to be a bit unbalanced, still.  I''m thinking if there were more negative space to the right and top *might* make it feel more balanced.<br/> <br/>Technically, generally speaking, the exposure, focus, etc is very well done.  Also, you have done well in teh bw conversion.  I think what might detract a bit is the top of the splash is not as sharp as the rest, or as distinct from rest of the sink.  In shots like this, it seems that people look around the rim of the water drop more than the base.  If the "rim" isn''t well focused, it takes away from the shot a bit.<br/> <br/>Overall, a good shot, and I can see the connection to the original. <br/> <br/>Best to you in future challenges.<br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Compositionally, I like that this is not centered, and that you have not "cut off" any of the drain (though that can work sometimes).  However, it seems to be a bit unbalanced, still.  I''m thinking if there were more negative space to the right and top *might* make it feel more balanced. Technically, generally speaking, the exposure, focus, etc is very well done.  Also, you have done well in teh bw conversion.  I think what might detract a bit is the top of the splash is not as sharp as the rest, or as distinct from rest of the sink.  In shots like this, it seems that people look around the rim of the water drop more than the base.  If the "rim" isn''t well focused, it takes away from the shot a bit. Overall, a good shot, and I can see the connection to the original.  Best to you in future challenges.Karma', '2009-02-21 21:42:27.000000', NULL, 0),
